  "explanation": "This presentation is typical of night terrors (sleep terrors): they occur in early sleep, are associated with abrupt screaming and inconsolability, and the child is usually difficult to comfort and has little or no recall afterward. Nightmares occur later in the night and are usually remembered; seizures are less likely to be recurrent, brief, and tightly linked to this pattern of partial arousal from sleep.",
